IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `esos-student`

-- Education Services for Overseas Students Act 2000 -- worked cases, from the overseas student's seat.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand from
-- the deposited text (C2025C00684), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario life raised this Act (REQ-0080 is a
-- scheduled priority-2 entry): the student (Priya, from India, enrolling in a two-year diploma in Perth) and the dates are the
-- encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 5.
#ASSERT `Am I an overseas student` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I am an overseas student (s 5)`
-- Before her visa is granted, having applied for the course.
#ASSERT `Am I an overseas student` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I am an intending overseas student (s 5)`
#ASSERT `Am I an overseas student` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am neither an overseas student nor an intending overseas student`
-- A visa holder of an excluded kind who still intends to become an overseas student.
#ASSERT `Am I an overseas student` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I am an intending overseas student (s 5)`

-- ss 8, 101.
#ASSERT `May this provider offer me the course (s 8)` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the provider is registered for this course at this location`
#ASSERT `May this provider offer me the course (s 8)` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the provider acts under an arrangement with a provider registered for this course at this location (s 8(2))`
#ASSERT `May this provider offer me the course (s 8)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: offering me this course would be an offence, because no registered provider for this course at this location stands behind it (s 8(1))`
#ASSERT `May this provider offer me the course (s 8)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: no one may offer or invite me to this course while an Immigration Minister's suspension certificate is in effect for the provider (s 101)`

-- s 27. Priya's diploma: 2 years (104 weeks), $36,000 in total.
#ASSERT `How much may my provider take before I start` 36000 104 FALSE EQUALS `no more than` 18000
#ASSERT `How much may my provider take before I start` 36000 104 TRUE EQUALS `no limit under s 27: I (or whoever pays my fees) chose to pay more than half`
-- A 20-week English course (ELICOS).
#ASSERT `How much may my provider take before I start` 8000 20 FALSE EQUALS `no limit under s 27: the course lasts 25 weeks or less`
-- 25 weeks exactly is "25 weeks or less".
#ASSERT `How much may my provider take before I start` 8000 25 FALSE EQUALS `no limit under s 27: the course lasts 25 weeks or less`
#ASSERT `How much may my provider take before I start` 8000 26 FALSE EQUALS `no more than` 4000

-- ss 28, 29, 31. A private college: yes. A public university with Commonwealth recurrent funding: exempt. After she starts: no.
#ASSERT `Must my provider hold my prepaid fees in a protected account` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT `Must my provider hold my prepaid fees in a protected account` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT (NOT `Must my provider hold my prepaid fees in a protected account` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (NOT `Must my provider hold my prepaid fees in a protected account` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT (NOT `Must my provider hold my prepaid fees in a protected account` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- s 19(1A). Priya (19) does not begin on 2 March 2027: report by 2 April 2027 (31 days).
#ASSERT `By when must my provider report it` `I did not begin my course when expected` (Date 2 3 2027) 19 EQUALS Date 2 4 2027
-- A 16-year-old school student: 14 days.
#ASSERT `By when must my provider report it` `I did not begin my course when expected` (Date 2 3 2027) 16 EQUALS Date 16 3 2027
#ASSERT `By when must my provider report it` `my studies ended before the course was completed` (Date 2 3 2027) 17 EQUALS Date 16 3 2027
-- A change of course for a 16-year-old is 31 days: only (c) and (d) are 14.
#ASSERT `By when must my provider report it` `my course, or its length, changed` (Date 2 3 2027) 16 EQUALS Date 2 4 2027

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 46A. The college does not start Priya's course on the agreed starting day, 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `Has my provider defaulted` `the provider did not start my course on the agreed starting day` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Has my provider defaulted` `my course stopped being provided after it started and before I completed it` FALSE FALSE
-- She had already withdrawn.
#ASSERT (NOT `Has my provider defaulted` `the provider did not start my course on the agreed starting day` TRUE FALSE)
-- The college stopped teaching her for non-payment: her default, not its (s 46A(3)).
#ASSERT (NOT `Has my provider defaulted` `my course stopped being provided after it started and before I completed it` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT (NOT `Has my provider defaulted` `my course went ahead as agreed` FALSE FALSE)

-- ss 46D, 49, 50A. Default day 1 March 2027: the provider has until 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `What do I get when my provider defaults` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 8 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS `my provider must, by the day given, either arrange a place in another course at its expense that I accept in writing, or refund my unspent tuition fees (s 46D)` (Date 15 3 2027)
#ASSERT `What do I get when my provider defaults` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 15 3 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS `my provider must, by the day given, either arrange a place in another course at its expense that I accept in writing, or refund my unspent tuition fees (s 46D)` (Date 15 3 2027)
-- It refunded her within the 14 days.
#ASSERT `What do I get when my provider defaults` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the provider has met its obligations to me (s 46D(3)); nothing is owed through the Tuition Protection Service`
-- It did nothing; the TPS Director knew by 16 March 2027: placement options, to be accepted by 14 April 2027 (30 days after 15 March).
#ASSERT `What do I get when my provider defaults` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 20 3 2027) FALSE (Date 16 3 2027) EQUALS `the TPS Director must offer me suitable alternative courses if any are available, which I may accept in writing by the day given, and the Tuition Fund pays the new provider or refunds me; my claim against the old provider ends (ss 49, 50A, 50B, 50C)` (Date 14 4 2027)
-- The TPS Director first learned of it on 1 March 2028, exactly 12 months on: not "more than 12 months".
#ASSERT `What do I get when my provider defaults` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 2 3 2028) FALSE (Date 1 3 2028) EQUALS `the TPS Director must offer me suitable alternative courses if any are available, which I may accept in writing by the day given, and the Tuition Fund pays the new provider or refunds me; my claim against the old provider ends (ss 49, 50A, 50B, 50C)` (Date 14 4 2027)
-- On 2 March 2028: too late for the Fund.
#ASSERT `What do I get when my provider defaults` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 5 3 2028) FALSE (Date 2 3 2028) EQUALS `nothing through the Tuition Protection Service: the TPS Director learned of the default more than 12 months after the default day (s 50A(5)); my claim against the provider remains (s 48)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- s 47A. Priya's course starts on 1 March 2027 but she does not turn up.
#ASSERT `Have I defaulted (s 47A)` `the course started on the agreed day but I did not start it` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 1 2000) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I have defaulted (s 47A), and the default day is` (Date 1 3 2027)
-- She did not start because the provider failed to start it.
#ASSERT `Have I defaulted (s 47A)` `the course started on the agreed day but I did not start it` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 1 1 2000) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: I did not start because the provider defaulted, so it is the provider's default (s 47A(2), s 46A)`
-- She withdraws on 10 May 2027.
#ASSERT `Have I defaulted (s 47A)` `I withdrew from the course` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 10 5 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I have defaulted (s 47A), and the default day is` (Date 10 5 2027)
-- Refused for misbehaviour without natural justice: not her default.
#ASSERT `Have I defaulted (s 47A)` `the provider refused to teach me for misbehaviour` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 10 5 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: a refusal for misbehaviour is not my default unless the provider first gave me natural justice (s 47A(3))`
#ASSERT `Have I defaulted (s 47A)` `the provider refused to teach me for misbehaviour` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 10 5 2027) FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I have defaulted (s 47A), and the default day is` (Date 10 5 2027)
#ASSERT `Have I defaulted (s 47A)` `the provider refused to teach me because I did not pay` (Date 1 3 2027) (Date 10 5 2027) FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I have defaulted (s 47A), and the default day is` (Date 10 5 2027)

-- ss 47D, 47E. She withdraws on 10 May 2027 under a compliant agreement and claims in writing on 12 May: refund by 9 June 2027.
#ASSERT `What refund must my provider pay after my default` (Date 10 5 2027) TRUE FALSE (Date 12 5 2027) EQUALS `a refund of the amount my written agreement sets, to me or the person it names, within 4 weeks after my written claim: by` (Date 9 6 2027)
-- No compliant agreement: the Minister's method, within 4 weeks after the default day: 7 June 2027.
#ASSERT `What refund must my provider pay after my default` (Date 10 5 2027) FALSE FALSE (Date 12 5 2027) EQUALS `a refund of the amount the Minister's instrument sets, to me, within 4 weeks after the default day: by` (Date 7 6 2027)
-- Her visa was refused and that is why she did not start (default day 1 March 2027): s 47E, by 29 March 2027.
#ASSERT `What refund must my provider pay after my default` (Date 1 3 2027) TRUE TRUE (Date 5 3 2027) EQUALS `a refund of the amount the Minister's instrument sets, to me, within 4 weeks after the default day: by` (Date 29 3 2027)

-- s 50A(4), (5).
#ASSERT `Will the Tuition Protection Service pay my refund` (Date 10 5 2027) (Date 9 6 2027) (Date 1 6 2027) FALSE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the refund is not overdue yet: the provider still has until the last day`
#ASSERT `Will the Tuition Protection Service pay my refund` (Date 10 5 2027) (Date 9 6 2027) (Date 20 6 2027) TRUE (Date 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the provider has paid the refund: nothing more is owed under Division 2`
#ASSERT `Will the Tuition Protection Service pay my refund` (Date 10 5 2027) (Date 9 6 2027) (Date 20 6 2027) FALSE (Date 15 6 2027) EQUALS `the TPS Director must pay me the refund from the Overseas Students Tuition Fund (or the person my agreement names), and my claim against the provider ends (ss 50A(4), 50B, 50C)`
#ASSERT `Will the Tuition Protection Service pay my refund` (Date 10 5 2027) (Date 9 6 2027) (Date 1 7 2028) FALSE (Date 11 5 2028) EQUALS `nothing through the Tuition Protection Service: the TPS Director learned of it more than 12 months after the default day (s 50A(5)); I may sue the provider for it as a debt (s 48)`
